Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:32:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] GDN conv-state gather fold: build_rs's GET_ROWS of the
 conv cache feeding a direct-conv CONCAT with the snapshot fold is deferred
 like the GDN state gather, and the direct kernel reads the cache row itself
 (row id = the gather's src[1]; the three state values sit in registers before
 the snapshot writes, one of which is the write-back to that row). Single
 sequence, <= 16 tokens, the CONCAT is the gather's only reader and only
 folded snapshot CPYs write the cache before the conv; a CONCAT over a
 deferred gather that the direct conv does not take aborts. Bit-identical.
 GGML_CUDA_FUSE_GDN_CONV_GATHER=0 off

